4:   "summary": "PASS for the scoped automated port task only. This is not full capstone acceptance. I could not execute code, so I did not re-run any acceptance checks myself.\n\nSCOPE OF MY WORK: I read the following.\n- loop/acceptance.md\n- the baseline result.json, tests.log and source.json\n- the coder handoff.json and process.json\n- platform/doomgeneric_wasm.c\n- web/index.html\n\nI did not read platform/doom_audio.c, web/audio.js, tests/*, loop/*.py or build.sh. I cannot vouch for those files beyond the baseline logs.\n\nEVIDENCE (paths under artifacts/runs/loop-20261105T010516Z-98b10905/):\n- baseline-c802e8a5/result.json: status PASS, source_digest db7ae64a828f0aacdb7a7e34d5e5faa4d0b3dd9acb832b52d556950250c9ba25. This matches the digest in my task.\n  - emcc 4.0.18 returned 0.\n  - build.sh returned 0.\n  - unittest discover returned 0.\n- baseline-c802e8a5/tests.log: 22 tests ran, OK.\n  - The audio test validated 13 MUS scores, truncation rejection and deferred audio initialization.\n  - The browser test passed all of these:\n    - WAD/Wasm load and rendered pixels\n    - sound gesture\n    - menu and new game\n    - simulation pacing\n    - movement, turning, and firing that consumes ammo\n    - nonzero SFX and music samples\n    - mute and volume\n    - use-key press and release\n    - synthetic blur\n    - WASD, strafe and run\n    - weapons and automap\n    - pause and resume\n    - no page, console or network errors\n  - The loop fixture tests passed.\n- baseline-c802e8a5/source.json: digest db7ae64a\u2026 and revision 1ba5d20.\n- integration-01-3a366236/coder/handoff.json: DONE with no changes. The coder said it made no edits, ran nothing, and did not read the source. process.json shows only returncode 0 and 18.15 s. I did not treat these as proof of anything.\n\nSTATIC REVIEW:\n- platform/doomgeneric_wasm.c checks for a valid IWAD and fails visibly if it is missing (:128-134).\n- The ring-buffer input in dg_key rejects bad keys and drops events when full (:83).\n- The BGR-to-RGBA conversion looks correct (:49-52).\n- The read-only observation exports are side-effect free.\n- web/index.html handles key aliases through the down map, so overlapping W/Up releases correctly (:52-69). It also releases keys on blur and when the page is hidden (:72-77), and it ignores button and input targets.\n- I found no correctness or regression defect in the files I read.\n\nRISKS (minor, not blocking):\n- The baseline ran at the same digest, but this reviewer pass did not independently confirm that the tests were fresh. The tester must run a fresh verification tied to db7ae64a\u2026 before the loop counts this task as complete.\n- Observation exports such as dg_in_level and dg_player_x read engine globals directly, so the tests depend on them.\n- Only a synthetic blur event is tested. There is no OS-level focus test.\n\nUNCOVERED (not established by the automated checks; do not treat as passed):\n- Door and switch activation in real gameplay.\n- Real OS focus transitions.\n- Physical speaker output and musical fidelity. Only nonzero-sample checks exist.\n- Save and config persistence across reloads. I saw no persistence layer in the files I read.\n- Mouse aiming. web/index.html has no mouse handlers, and the coder said the mouse code in i_input.c is commented out. Mouse aiming is not implemented or tested.\n- Manual playthrough. This has not been performed and I did not invent it.\n\nFULL ASSIGNMENT, NOT ESTABLISHED:\n- The blind teammate/instructor regression repair exercise is NOT PERFORMED. The user asked to omit it.\n- Live resumption on real runs. test_loop.py covers fixtures only.\n- Design rationale and reflection write-ups.\n- Historical token and cost usage remains unknown.\n\nUNRESOLVED DEFECTS: none found in the scoped port.",
